Task 2: Dynamic Profitability Model Analysis

Overview

A dynamic profitability model was developed to evaluate the financial viability of Amazon advertising campaigns. The model calculates revenue, profit, ACOS, TACOS, and break-even points based on user-defined inputs.

Base Scenario

Inputs:

- Selling Price: ₹800
- COGS: ₹280
- Amazon Referral Fee: 12%
- Monthly Ad Spend: ₹300,000
- Ad Units Sold: 1,500
- Organic Units Sold: 2,000
- Fixed Costs: ₹150,000

Results:

- Gross Margin: ₹520
- Amazon Fee: ₹96
- Ad Cost per Unit: ₹200
- Net Margin (Ad Unit): ₹224
- Net Margin (Organic Unit): ₹424
- Total Revenue: ₹2,800,000
- Monthly Profit: ₹1,034,000
- ACOS: 25%
- TACOS: 10.71%

Scenario Analysis

Price Increase (₹950)

Increasing the selling price improves revenue and profitability while reducing TACOS.

Cost Increase (+20% COGS)

Higher product costs reduce margins and decrease overall profitability.

Organic Growth (3,500 Units)

Increased organic sales improve profit and reduce TACOS without additional advertising spend.

Competitive Pricing (₹700 SP)

Reducing price decreases profit margins and may require stronger advertising performance to maintain profitability.

Conclusion

The model demonstrates that long-term profitability depends on balancing pricing strategy, advertising efficiency, operational costs, and organic growth. While advertising drives visibility and sales, sustainable growth comes from improving margins and increasing organic revenue.
